"""DRV8874PWPR - 4.5-37 V, 6 A peak brushed DC H-bridge with current sense and regulation. Bare part.

Datasheet: TI SLVSF66A (August 2019, revised December 2019), "DRV8874 H-Bridge Motor Driver With
Integrated Current Sense and Regulation". Package HTSSOP-16 PowerPAD (PWP0016J, 5.0 x 4.4 mm
body, section 12). Orderable part DRV8874PWPR: tape and reel, 3000 (Package Option Addendum).

Pins (section 5, Pin Functions, p3): 1 EN/IN1, 2 PH/IN2, 3 nSLEEP, 4 nFAULT, 5 VREF, 6 IPROPI,
7 IMODE, 8 OUT1, 9 PGND, 10 OUT2, 11 VM, 12 VCP, 13 CPH, 14 CPL, 15 GND, 16 PMODE, thermal PAD
(footprint pad 17). GND, PGND and PAD go to one GND io: Pin Functions ("Connect to system
ground") and section 10.1 ("PGND and GND should connect together directly on the PCB ground
plane. They are not intended to be isolated from each other").

Absolute maximum ratings (section 6.1, p4): VM -0.3 to 40 V; CPH, VCP VM - 0.3 to VM + 7 V; CPL
-0.3 to VM + 0.3 V; EN/IN1, PH/IN2, nSLEEP, IMODE, PMODE and nFAULT -0.3 to 5.75 V; IPROPI -0.3 to
5.75 V and to VM + 0.3 V; VREF -0.3 to 5.75 V; OUTx -0.9 to VM + 0.9 V; GND to PGND +-0.3 V; TJ
-40 to 150 C.

Recommended operating conditions (section 6.3, p4): VM 4.5 to 37 V; logic inputs 0 to 5.5 V;
fPWM 0 to 100 kHz on EN/IN1, PH/IN2; nFAULT pull-up voltage 0 to 5.5 V and sink current IOD up to
5 mA; peak output current 6 A ("power dissipation and thermal limits must be observed"); IPROPI
output current 0 to 3 mA; VREF 0 to 3.6 V. Thermal (section 6.4): RthJA 36.0 C/W, RthJC(bot)
2.7 C/W on the JEDEC board.

Electrical characteristics (section 6.5, p5-6):
- RDS(on) 100 mOhm typ, 120 mOhm max per FET (high side and low side, VM 24 V, 2 A, TJ 25 C):
  200 / 240 mOhm across the bridge. Body diode 0.9 V; tRISE/tFALL 150 ns, tPD 400 ns, tDEAD
  100 ns (VM 24 V).
- Logic inputs: VIL 0.7 V (VM < 5 V) or 0.8 V (VM >= 5 V) max, VIH 1.5 V min; 100 kOhm pull-down
  to GND (Figure 16), so an open EN/IN1, PH/IN2 or nSLEEP reads low.
- PMODE tri-level (Table 2, section 7.3.2): VTIL 0 to 0.65 V -> PH/EN mode; VTIZ 0.9-1.2 V (left
  open: 44 kOhm to GND and 156 kOhm to the internal 5 V, Figure 17) -> independent half-bridge;
  VTIH 1.5 to 5.5 V -> PWM mode.
- IMODE quad-level (Table 6, section 7.3.3.2): level 1 tied to GND (0-0.45 V) -> fixed off-time,
  automatic retry, nFAULT on faults only; level 2 20 kOhm to GND (18.6-21.4 kOhm) ->
  cycle-by-cycle, automatic retry, nFAULT also on every chop; level 3 62 kOhm to GND
  (57.6-66.4 kOhm) -> cycle-by-cycle, latched off; level 4 Hi-Z (or 2.5-5.5 V) -> fixed off-time,
  latched off. Internal 136 kOhm to GND and 68 kOhm to 5 V (Figure 18).
- PMODE and IMODE are latched when nSLEEP takes the device out of sleep (sections 7.3.2,
  7.3.3.2, 7.4.1).
- Current mirror AIPROPI 450 uA/A typ, error AERR +-5.5 % (2-4 A), +-6 % (1-2 A), +-7.5 %
  (0.4-1 A), +-30 mA below 0.4 A, VM 5.5-37 V. IPROPI = (ILS1 + ILS2) x AIPROPI (equation 1):
  it mirrors the low-side FETs only, so it reads in drive and in brake (slow decay) but not in
  coast (section 7.3.3.1).
- Current regulation: ITRIP x AIPROPI = VVREF / RIPROPI (equation 3); tOFF 25 us, tBLK 1.1 us,
  tDEG 0.6 us, tDELAY 1.6 us. In fixed off-time mode an input edge during tOFF ends it
  (section 7.3.3.2.1). Regulation is disabled with PMODE Hi-Z, or by tying IPROPI to GND with
  VREF above GND (section 7.3.3.2).
- Protection: UVLO 4.3 / 4.45 / 4.6 V rising, 4.2 / 4.35 / 4.5 V falling; CPUV 2.25 V; OCP
  IOCP 6 A min, 10 A typ (no maximum), tOCP 3 us deglitch, tRETRY 2 ms; TSD 160 / 175 / 190 C,
  20 C hysteresis. Every fault pulls nFAULT low (Table 7).
- nFAULT is open drain (Pin Functions "OD"): VOL 0.3 V max at 5 mA, IOZ +-2 uA.
- nSLEEP: low -> sleep (outputs Hi-Z, IVMQ under 1 uA at 24 V, 25 C); tWAKE and tSLEEP 1 ms max.

Truth tables (section 7.3.2): PH/EN (PMODE low, Table 3): EN = 0 brake (both low sides on),
EN = 1 and PH = 1 forward (OUT1 high), PH = 0 reverse. PWM (PMODE high, Table 4): IN1 = IN2 = 0
coast (Hi-Z), 1 0 forward, 0 1 reverse, 1 1 brake.

External parts (integrator-owned; Table 1, section 7.3.1; section 9.1; section 10.1):
- CVM1 0.1 uF low-ESR ceramic VM to GND, VM-rated; CVM2 bulk capacitance, VM-rated (no value:
  section 9.1 leaves it to system testing).
- CVCP 100 nF X5R/X7R 16 V from VCP to VM; CFLY 22 nF X5R/X7R VM-rated from CPH to CPL. All
  close to the pins (section 10.1).
- RIPROPI from IPROPI to GND; VREF from a divider on the controller supply (Figure 19).
- RIMODE, RPMODE straps; RnFAULT pull-up with IOD <= 5 mA.
- Thermal pad to the ground planes through thermal vias (section 10.1; the land pattern's via
  grid, p40); maximise the copper on the pad.

The netlist rules a board must meet are checked by `checks.zen` (see its docstring).
"""

# Section 6.3, p4: recommended operating range of VM.
VM = io(Power(voltage="4.5V to 37V"))
GND = io(Ground)
VCP = io(Net)
CPH = io(Net)
CPL = io(Net)
EN_IN1 = io(Net)
PH_IN2 = io(Net)
NSLEEP = io(Net)
NFAULT = io(Net)
VREF = io(Net)
IPROPI = io(Net)
IMODE = io(Net)
PMODE = io(Net)
OUT1 = io(Net)
OUT2 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="DRV8874",
    prefix="IC",
    symbol=Symbol(library="DRV8874.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("Texas_PWP0016J_HTSSOP-16-1EP_4.4x5mm_P0.65mm_EP3.4x5mm_Mask2.46x3.55mm.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="DRV8874PWPR", manufacturer="Texas Instruments"),
    pins={
        "EN/IN1": EN_IN1,
        "PH/IN2": PH_IN2,
        "~{SLEEP}": NSLEEP,
        "~{FAULT}": NFAULT,
        "VREF": VREF,
        "IPROPI": IPROPI,
        "IMODE": IMODE,
        "OUT1": OUT1,
        "PGND": GND,
        "OUT2": OUT2,
        "VM": VM,
        "VCP": VCP,
        "CPH": CPH,
        "CPL": CPL,
        "GND": GND,
        "PMODE": PMODE,
        "PAD": GND,
    },
)
